                                          owl:someValuesFrom obo:CHEBI_33250
                                        ] ;
                        dcterms:description "Oxidation state is an atomic descriptor that gives the degree of oxidation of an atom in terms of counting electrons. The higher the oxidation state (OS) of a given atom, the greater is its degree of oxidation. [source: IUPAC Gold Book - https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.O04365]" ;
